# The SSH key that signs SHA256SUMS of every release (RELEASES.md).
#
# Verify a release with:
#
#   ssh-keygen -Y verify -f allowed_signers -I 0xoucanxxx@gmail.com \
#       -n file -s SHA256SUMS.sig < SHA256SUMS
#
# Take this file from the git repository at the release's tag, not from the
# release page: a file published next to the signature it vouches for proves
# nothing. Compare the key with a second channel too before trusting it: it
# is one of the maintainer's keys at https://github.com/0xOucan.keys.
#
# Rotating the key: the new key is added here in a commit, announced, and
# noted in the changelog; the announcement of the new key is signed with the
# old one. Releases already published stay verifiable with the line at their
# own tag.
0xoucanxxx@gmail.com namespaces="file" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIAPljmoBLnjaqSUF/ThaMU5dcuolTHq4t3sG0991BZwF
